{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An attached macro emits a small record into a section LinkerSets owns, and a typed run-time API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"enumerates every record of one kind in a deterministic order. Each record carries a kind, so"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"clients share the mechanism without seeing each other’s records. Failures are typed errors; the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"run-time API never traps."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A declaration registers itself with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", tagged with a kind: four ASCII"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"characters read as a 32-bit integer. A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/documentation\/LinkerSetsRuntime\/LinkerSet","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" of that kind finds every such declaration"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"at run time:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["import LinkerSets","","enum Routes {","    @LinkerSetEntry(kind: 0x726F_7574)  \/\/ \"rout\"","    static let home = Route(path: \"\/\")","}","","let routes = LinkerSet<Route>(kind: LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x726F_7574)).values"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A client that registers one kind of thing can give it a macro with the kind fixed, such as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route"},{"type":"text","text":", from its own compiler plugin. The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation shows"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"how."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Guides","title":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/Performance"]},{"anchor":"Declaring-records","title":"Declaring records","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetEntry(kind:)"]},{"anchor":"Macros","generated":true,"title":"Macros","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/linkerSetRecord(kind:storing:)"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"LinkerSets","externalID":"LinkerSets"},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/ReplacingARegistry":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry","kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"abstract":[{"text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says